mdx"},{"$id":"contribute/bazel.mdx","type":"page","name":"Develop with Bazel","description":"Build, test, and run Forge with Bazel, the same dev loop CI uses.","icon":"$undefined","url":"/contribute/bazel","$ref":"contribute/bazel.mdx"},{"$id":"contribute/cargo.mdx","type":"page","name":"Developing with Cargo","description":"Pure Cargo workflow for Forge contributors who'd rather not run Bazel.","icon":"$undefined","url":"/contribute/cargo","$ref":"contribute/cargo.mdx"},{"$id":"contribute/nix.mdx","type":"page","name":"Develop with Nix","description":"The dev shell that generates the bazelrc files the rest of the build assumes, and what is actually inside it.","icon":"$undefined","url":"/contribute/nix","$ref":"contribute/nix.mdx"},{"$id":"contribute/repo-crate-map.mdx","type":"page","name":"Repository and crate map","description":"What every crate and top-level directory in the Forge repository is for, and which one your change belongs in.","icon":"$undefined","url":"/contribute/repo-crate-map","$ref":"contribute/repo-crate-map.mdx"},{"$id":"contribute/codebase-internals.mdx","type":"page","name":"Codebase internals","description":"The traits, the error model, the async rules and the two metric systems: the conventions a reviewer will assume you already know.","icon":"$undefined","url":"/contribute/codebase-internals","$ref":"contribute/codebase-internals.mdx"},{"$id":"contribute/how-to-extend.mdx","type":"page","name":"How to extend Forge","description":"Complete file-by-file recipes for adding a store, a config field, a metric, or a gRPC service.","icon":"$undefined","url":"/contribute/how-to-extend","$ref":"contribute/how-to-extend.mdx"},{"$id":"contribute/testing-guide.mdx","type":"page","name":"Testing guide","description":"How Forge's tests are organised, what `#[forge_test]` gives you, and which local environment problems cause which confusing failure.","icon":"$undefined","url":"/contribute/testing-guide","$ref":"contribute/testing-guide.mdx"},{"$id":"cont